  "note": "Triennial election of the Ballycastle Urban District Council, polled Wednesday 20 May 1964. Seventeen candidates contested twelve seats after three Independent withdrawals; the Unionists lost a seat and the Nationalists gained one (Belfast News-Letter, 22 May 1964, p. 12). Patrick Dallat and Robert O'Connor were new members."
